Eligible authors and balance pool: all nine Justices. The minimum is five and no count exceeds six. The Chief selects Kennedy, count five. Fit governs: his Sullivan particular-choice inquiry and Edmonson public-machinery analysis directly address the case's hardest boundary, distinguishing private medical choice from an actual governmental confinement function without minimizing the liberty deprivation. His formulation preserves West's delegated-duty exception and applies separately to referral/transport and certification/confinement. Ginsburg offers a strong alternative through Carter's separation of deprivation from attribution but has six leads; Kennedy can carry the same safeguards with the lower count. Stone's approved formulation is fully compatible but supplies no distinct coalition accommodation or comparative advantage requiring self-assignment. One counted signed plenary lead accrues to Kennedy after this Record is written.

